    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d317-a6">

                <pb facs="0433" n="325" sameAs="frus:frus1893/pg325"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[<hi rendition="#italic">Extract from minutes of a
                            court held for trial of Eno, a British subject</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">native of Raratonga</hi>), <hi rendition="#italic"
                            >trading for Albert Kustel, an American subject.—Ed. H. M. Davis,
                            captain.</hi>]</seg></opener>
                <p rendition="#center">* * * * * * *</p>
                <p>4. For that the said Eno did burn down the house of Jacob, a native of
                    Tarawa.</p>
                <p rendition="#center">* * * * * * *</p>
                <p>The statements of the natives referred to in the charges having been read, the
                    accused was asked whether he admitted or denied the truth of them. He admitted
                    the truth of the charges, but said * * * with reference to the 4th charge, he
                    was ordered to do it by Kustel.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Ed. H. M. Davis</hi>,<lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">Captain H. M. S. Royalist, and one of Her Majesty’s
                            Deputy Commissioners.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
